# HighRise tables — layout & toolbar placement

Every data table (crawled pages, found resources, source inventory, competitor
leaderboards, prompt inventory, etc.) must follow the shared HighRise
`HLDataTable` layout and the same toolbar element placement. Consistency across
tables matters more than per-screen creativity.

## Toolbar element placement (non-negotiable)

The table toolbar is a single row: **filters on the left, search + actions on the right.**

```
[ filter pills ] [ Advanced/Add filter ] ............ [ Search ] [ Columns ] [ primary action ]
        └── left group ──┘                              └────────── right group (ml-auto) ──────────┘
```

- Put every filter control on the **left**: filter pills / segmented filters
  (e.g. `All sources | Mentioned | Not mentioned`), status filter chips, and the
  `Advanced filter` trigger (use shared `AdvancedFilterTrigger` — see
  `advanced-filter` rule; Crawled pages is the reference).
- Put **search on the right**, followed by `Columns` and any primary CTA
  (`Apply fixes`, etc.). Right-align the group with `ml-auto`.
- Never put search on the left / filters on the right. Never split filters across
  both sides.
- The row is one flex line: `flex items-center gap-2 flex-wrap`, with the right
  group started by `ml-auto`.

## Control sizing

- Toolbar controls are **sm / 32px tall** (`h-8`) with **8px corners** (`rounded-lg`).
- Search input follows the canonical input (see the input-field rule): `h-8`,
  `rounded-lg`, `border-gray-300`, `text-[14px]`, `focus:border-primary-600`, with
  a leading `Search` icon (`pl-9`). Give it a fixed width (~240–280px), not `flex-1`.
- Filter chips / Advanced filter: `text-[14px]` (see `filter-styles` rule).
- `Columns` buttons: `h-8 px-3 rounded-lg bg-gray-100`, `text-[14px] font-medium`
  (never 12px / 13px).

## Reference implementation

`CrawledPagesTab` in `src/components/dashboards/SiteHealthDashboard.jsx` is the
canonical toolbar: filters on the left, then `<div className="ml-auto flex items-center gap-2">`
holding search + `Columns`. Match it when building or fixing any table toolbar.

## Header hierarchy (non-negotiable)

Two header styles only, based on nesting depth. Always sentence case, never
`uppercase` / `tracking-wide` (see the sentence-casing rule).

- **Top-level (parent) table headers** — `text-[12px] font-semibold text-gray-900`
  (`#101828`). This is every standalone / parent `<th>` across all dashboards.
- **Nested-in-row table headers** — `text-[12px] font-medium text-gray-900`
  (`#101828`). Used for any data table rendered inside an expandable row.
  Same size as parent headers, differentiated by weight (medium vs semibold).

## Nested data tables (inside expandable rows) — single design

Any data table shown when a row is expanded MUST use this one design — the Found
resources source-details table in `src/components/dashboards/SiteHealthDashboard.jsx`
is the canonical reference. No other nested-table design is allowed.

- Layout: inset via `flex pb-3 pr-4` with a leading spacer matching the expand
  column (`TABLE_EXPAND_COL`), then a card
  `flex-1 min-w-0 rounded-lg border border-gray-100 bg-white overflow-x-auto`.
- Table: `w-full border-collapse text-left`.
- Header row: `bg-gray-50/80 border-b border-gray-100`; header cells
  `px-4 py-2.5 text-[12px] font-medium text-gray-900` (+ `whitespace-nowrap` /
  `min-w` as needed).
- Body rows: `border-b border-gray-50 last:border-0 hover:bg-gray-50/40`; body
  cells `px-4 py-2.5 text-[12px] text-gray-600`; link cells
  `text-[12px] font-medium text-primary-600 hover:underline truncate`.
- Interactive nested tables (selection checkboxes, editable value / Fix CTAs) keep
  their controls but must adopt the same wrapper / header / row chrome.

## Table body conventions

- Expandable rows keep the expand chevron + checkbox in one fixed vertical line
  across parent and nested content (`TABLE_EXPAND_COL` / `TABLE_CHECK_COL`).
- Select-all headers use the indeterminate `TableCheckbox` pattern.
- Count / metric cards above a table use the shared `CountCard` (see count-card rule).

## Before finishing table work

- [ ] Filters on the left, search + actions on the right (`ml-auto`).
- [ ] Controls are `h-8` + `rounded-lg`; search uses the canonical input.
- [ ] Parent headers are sentence-case, `text-[12px] font-semibold text-gray-900`.
- [ ] Nested-row tables use the single reference design with
      `text-[12px] font-medium text-gray-900` headers.
- [ ] Reused shared table patterns instead of a bespoke layout.
